    "content": "The University of Michigan men’s basketball team has won one NCAA National Championship, defeating Seton Hall 80–79 in overtime in 1989. The Wolverines have appeared in seven NCAA championship games (1965, 1976, 1989, 1992, 1993, 2013, 2018). 1989 NCAA Championship Final Score: Michigan 80, Seton Hall 79 (OT) Coach: Steve Fisher (interim) Most Outstanding Player (MOP): Glen Rice Key Performers: Glen Rice (31 points), Rumeal Robinson (21 points) Key Tournament History Final Four Appearances: 8 (1964, 1965, 1976, 1989, 1992, 1993, 2013, 2018) Championship Game Losses: 1965 (vs. UCLA), 1976 (vs. Indiana), 1992 (vs. Duke), 1993 (vs. North Carolina), 2013 (vs. Louisville), 2018 (vs. Villanova) Vacated Games: The 1992 and 1993 Final Four appearances, including the championship game losses by the \"Fab Five,\" were vacated by the NCAA due to sanctions. The 1989 team is remembered for its high-scoring offense, averaging 91.7 points per game.",
